name unicode-bidi-character-tests
# BidiCharacterTest.txt's header defines the input, paragraph direction,
# resolved paragraph level, per-character levels and visual ordering.
# A resolution belongs to the whole input in its requested direction. Its
# ordered level and index paths stay together, including X9's x markers.
# The operation's name is the header's "Unicode Bidirectional Algorithm".
match BidiCharacterTest.txt
format lp_bidi_character
codepoints input
content direction paragraph_level level index
thing record input direction
thing level .
thing index .
thing levels of level
thing visual_order of index
thing resolution paragraph_level levels visual_order preserve
# An empty visual order means every input character was removed by rule X9.
thing resolution paragraph_level levels preserve
relation "Unicode Bidirectional Algorithm" resolution
holds record resolution
